      <data key="d5">resumen</data>
      <data key="d6">en</data>
      <data key="d7">This article reports a participatory evaluation of a telehealth program with rural caregivers, community leaders and primary care teams. External academic and non-academic actors participated actively in defining the problem, implementing the service and evaluating the results. Workshops identified needs, tested the service and discussed changes in access to support.</data>
